          "filename": "Browns Canyon National Monument, CO (30180529841).jpg",
          "caption": "One fourth of the lands – 58 million acres -- managed by the BLM are forests or woodlands. These make up an important part of the BLM’s multiple-use mission and are managed for a variety of critical uses for the benefit of all Americans. Forest and woodland management produces traditional products such as lumber, plywood, and paper as well as other uses such as poles, greenery, biomass for energy production, and fuelwood for personal use while maintaining high-quality wildlife habitat.\nPhoto Credit: Bob Wick/BLM",
